## Example incident (anonymised)

A `SessionRepository.currentSession: Flow<Session?>` was added in week 1. Initial PR had one observer in `MainActivity`; tests passed. Week 8 a notification feature added a second observer in `NotificationService`. Symptoms:
- Notifications lost the user identity when switching from foreground → background → foreground (NotificationService re-collected, cold flow restarted, no replay)
- `MainActivity` and `NotificationService` saw different user objects for ~200ms after login (separate pipelines, separate DB queries with slightly different timing)

Fix: changed `Flow<Session?>` to `StateFlow<Session?>` with `MutableStateFlow` backing in the repository implementation. All downstream observers (now 4) share the same hot state. Reconnection storm eliminated.

iOS counterpart: changed `AnyPublisher<Session?, Never>` constructed from a one-shot `Just(...)` chain to be backed by `@Published var session: Session?` in the repository's observable container.
